            <title>[LU-20953] sanity-lnet test_238: FAIL 'Failed to ping &lt;IP&gt;@tcp1'</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20953</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-lnet test_238 failed with 'Failed to ping 10.240.29.32@tcp1' on change 69422 patchset 3 (&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/7ffaad0a-e38d-4ee3-8d4a-a2d63dce5b89" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/7ffaad0a-e38d-4ee3-8d4a-a2d63dce5b89&lt;/a&gt;), review-ldiskfs-arm, Rocky 9.8 aarch64. The same signature failed in the last 30 days on two unrelated changes, neither part of this series: 69203 patchset 1 (10.240.28.232@tcp1, 2026-09-25) and 68158 patchset 24 (10.240.22.241@tcp1, 2026-09-25). No existing ticket covers this error: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20425" title="sanity-lnet test_238: Timeout occurred after 397 minutes, last suite running was sanity-lnet" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20425"&gt;LU-20425&lt;/a&gt; covers a test_238 timeout and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20630" title="sanity-lnet test_238: FAIL 'Expect Multi-Rail: false, found False' when the router runs &amp;lt; 2.16" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20630"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20630&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (resolved) covers a Multi-Rail string mismatch, both different failures of the same test. Change 69422 patchset 3 touches only lustre/lod and lustre/obdclass RR target selection code, unrelated to LNet networking, so this test and its diff do not intersect. This looks like an ambient ping or connectivity flake in the test infrastructure. Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69422-ps3-d8a2a035b833 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69422" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69422&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
